    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The Image du Monde Challenge, was a two-week competition pitting five international teams of scholars against each other in a race to transcribe five copies of one text, the mid-thirteenth century verse treatise, Image du Monde, by Gossuin (or Gautier) du Metz. This challenge will took place in two parts; Part 1 occurred between September 25-October 9, 2020, and Part II occurred in early January 2021.\r\n\r\nThis project is inspired by La Sfera Challenge, a competition to transcribe eight copies of Goro Dati’s fifteenth-century geographic treatise, La Sfera. It had two iterations: the first involved three teams from May 22-June 5, 2020 and the second between five teams from July 17-31, 2020. The competitions played out on Twitter at #LaSferaChallenge and #LaSferaChallenge2.\r\n\r\nSupport for the project comes from the IIIF Consortium, FromThePage, and Stanford Libraries.\r\n\r\nWatch how the challenge progresses by following the Twitter hashtag #ImageduMonde!",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
